{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_58243","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["5\u0027-O-[(sulfonatooxy)phosphinato]adenosine","5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate dianion","adenosine 5\u0027-phosphosulfate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_58243","description":["An organic dianion arising from deprotonation of the phosphate and sufate groups of 5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate; major species at pH 7.3."],"label":"5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate(2-)","obo_id":"CHEBI:58243","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["5\u0027-O-[(sulfonatooxy)phosphinato]adenosine"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17709","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["5\u0027-Adenylyl sulfate","5\u0027-adenylyl hydrogen sulfate","ADENOSINE-5\u0027-PHOSPHOSULFATE","APS","Adenosine 5\u0027-phosphosulfate","Adenylylsulfate","adenosine phosphosulfate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_17709","description":["An adenosine 5\u0027-phosphate having a sulfo group attached to one the phosphate OH groups."],"label":"5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate","obo_id":"CHEBI:17709","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["5\u0027-adenylyl hydrogen sulfate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_58339","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["3\u0027-O-phosphonato-5\u0027-O-[(sulfonatooxy)phosphinato]adenosine","3\u0027-phosphoadenylyl sulfate","3\u0027-phosphonato-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate tetraanion","3\u0027-phosphonato-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate","3\u0027-phosphonatoadenosine 5\u0027-phosphosulfate tetraanion","3\u0027-phosphonatoadenosine 5\u0027-phosphosulfate","3\u0027-phosphonatoadenosine 5\u0027-phosphosulfate(4-)","PAPS tetraanion","PAPS","PAPS(4-)"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_58339","description":["A quadruply-charged organophosphate oxoanion arising from deprotonation of the phosphate and sufate groups of 3\u0027-phosphonato-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate; major species at pH 7.3."],"label":"3\u0027-phosphonato-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate(4-)","obo_id":"CHEBI:58339","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["3\u0027-O-phosphonato-5\u0027-O-[(sulfonatooxy)phosphinato]adenosine"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_848","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["2\u0027-O-phosphono-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate","2\u0027-Phosphoadenylylsulfate","2\u0027-phosphoadenylyl sulfate","5\u0027-O-[hydroxy(sulfooxy)phosphoryl]adenosine 2\u0027-(dihydrogen phosphate)"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_848","description":["An adenosine bisphosphate having monophosphate groups at the 2\u0027- and 5\u0027-positions and a sulfo group attached to the phosphate at position 5\u0027."],"label":"2\u0027-phospho-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate","obo_id":"CHEBI:848","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["2\u0027-O-phosphono-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate","5\u0027-O-[hydroxy(sulfooxy)phosphoryl]adenosine 2\u0027-(dihydrogen phosphate)"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17980","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["3\u0027-O-phosphono-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate","3\u0027-Phospho-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate","3\u0027-Phosphoadenosine 5\u0027-phosphosulfate","3\u0027-Phosphoadenylyl sulfate","3\u0027-phospho-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate","3\u0027-phosphoadenosine 5\u0027-phosphosulfate","PAPS"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_17980","description":["An adenosine bisphosphate having monophosphate groups at the 3\u0027- and 5\u0027-positions and a sulfo group attached to the phosphate at position 5\u0027."],"label":"3\u0027-phospho-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate","obo_id":"CHEBI:17980","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["3\u0027-O-phosphono-5\u0027-adenylyl sulfate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C47605","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C47605","description":["The sulfate salt form of metaproterenol, a short-acting and selective sympathomimetic beta-receptor agonist with bronchodilator activity. Metaproterenol sulfate binds beta-2 adrenergic receptors in bronchial smooth muscle and stimulates intracellular adenyl cyclase, thereby increasing the production of cyclic adenosine monophosphate (cAMP). Increased cAMP levels cause relaxation of bronchial smooth muscle, improve mucocliary clearance and reduce inflammatory cell mediator release, especially from mast cells."],"label":"Metaproterenol Sulfate","obo_id":"NCIT:C47605","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["1,3-Benzenediol, 5-(1-hydroxy-2-((1-methylethyl)amino)ethyl)-, Sulfate(2:1)(Salt)","3,5-Dihydroxy-alpha-((isopropylamino)methyl)benzyl Alcohol Sulfate","Alupent","METAPROTERENOL SULFATE","Metaproterenol Sulfate","Novasmasol"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C65983","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C65983","description":["The sulfate salt form of isoproterenol, a beta-adrenergic receptor agonist with bronchodilator activity. Isoproterenol binds to beta-2 adrenergic receptors in bronchial smooth muscle, thereby activating intracellular adenyl cyclase, an enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of adenosine triphosphate (ATP) to cyclic-3\u0027,5\u0027-adenosine monophosphate (cAMP). Increased cAMP levels cause relaxation of bronchial smooth muscle, relieve bronchospasms, improve mucociliary clearance and inhibit the release of mediators of immediate hypersensitivity from cells, especially from mast cells."],"label":"Isoproterenol Sulfate","obo_id":"NCIT:C65983","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ISOPROTERENOL SULFATE","Isoproterenol Sulfate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C47957","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C47957","description":["The sulfate salt of the short-acting sympathomimetic agent albuterol, a 1:1 racemic mixture of (R)-albuterol and (S)-albuterol with bronchodilator activity. Albuterol stimulates beta2-adrenergic receptors in the lungs, thereby activating the enzyme adenylate cyclase that catalyzes the conversion of ATP to cyclic-3\u0027,5\u0027-adenosine monophosphate (cAMP). Increased cAMP concentrations relax bronchial smooth muscle, relieve bronchospasms, and reduce inflammatory cell mediator release, especially from mast cells. To a lesser extent albuterol stimulates beta1-adrenergic receptors, thereby increasing the force and rate of myocardial contraction."],"label":"Albuterol Sulfate","obo_id":"NCIT:C47957","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["ALBUTEROL SULFATE","Albuterol Sulfate","Proventil","Salbutamol Sulphate","Ventolin"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C152913","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C152913","description":["The sulfate salt form of vorapaxar, an orally bioavailable protease-activated receptor-1 (PAR-1) antagonist, with antiplatelet activity. Upon oral administration, vorapaxar binds to PAR-1 expressed on platelets, and inhibits PAR-1-mediated platelet aggregation. Vorapaxar inhibits thrombin-induced and thrombin receptor agonist peptide (TRAP)-induced platelet aggregation, and does not inhibit platelet aggregation induced by adenosine diphosphate (ADP), collagen or a thromboxane mimetic."],"label":"Vorapaxar Sulfate","obo_id":"NCIT:C152913","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["SCH 530348","VORAPAXAR SULFATE","Vorapaxar Sulfate","Zontivity"]}],"numFound":9,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["CHEBI","5","NCIT","4"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","9"],"ontologyId":["ec","82","go","61","rexo","45","cco","45","gexo","45","reto","45","pr","9","upheno","7","mesh","7","slm","5","chebi","5","ncit","4","micro","3","medgen","2","snomed","2","upa","2","ordo","1","obi","1","pcl","1","dideo","1","one","1"],"ontologyIri":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/chebi.owl","5","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncit.owl","4"],"isObsolete":["false","9"],"type":["class","9"]}}}